in 2019 elita battle angel  a gorgeous cyberpunk adventure was  unleashed upon the world  featuring a wide-eyed cyborg in a  corrupt world  this visually packed film lends itself  to re-watching  in fact there are some things you might  only notice after a second viewing  and we're here to revisit those moments  the dystopian 26th century setting of  elita battle angel  comes complete with a floating sky city  killer sports  advanced robotics and even a bit of  chocolate  that's so great however hundreds of  years of technological advancement  have blurred the line between human and  machine by the time elita steps out onto  the bustling streets of iron city  you've probably already acclimated to  the cgi heavy details of her design  cybernetic limb replacements are  commonplace in this world  in fact many of the characters are so  heavily modified  that the only organic component left in  them seems to be their brains  as more characters enter the fray  viewers don't even realize on their  first watch of the film  that there might actually be more cgi  enhanced figures than there are plain  old human actors  excluding the innumerable extras  wandering around in the background  few elita characters aren't part machine  by the time we reach the finale  even elita's love interest hugo  eventually has his head transferred to a  cyborg body  the movie's ability to pull you into  this cyberpunk reality is thanks to its  top-notch cgi  that's not a surprise considering the  talent and experience behind the film  james cameron the film's producer and  co-screenwriter  worked on the spectacular visuals for  more than a decade  the central metaphor in elita is blatant  the human elite  live in the floating city of salem and  dump their trash  into the city below where the rest of  humanity lives  most of iron city's population is either  desperately trying to scrape by or  working feverishly to move to the city  above  elita is repeatedly told that no one  ever ascends to life in xalam  despite people's belief in the  possibility it just doesn't seem to  happen  however the cargo tubes that ship  materials up to xalam  seem to be a viable way of sneaking in  the prospect even comes up in  conversation  but is dismissed when hugo informs elita  about the world around her  he describes the tubes as meant for  cargo not people and the topic doesn't  come up again  while the concept of sneaking into xalam  through a cargo tube seems pretty  obvious  it must be extremely hazardous whatever  future gizmo  zips cargo around could probably crush a  human or a cyborg body  also it might be pressurized in some  lethal way but our vast knowledge of  heist movies has us thinking there are  more possibilities here than hugo might  realize  however after hugo has his cyborg body  he tackles the tubes from another angle  and decides to just walk on top of one  all the way to xalum  unfortunately he didn't expect his  stroll to be cut tragically short by  spinning blades of death  elita's introduction into the world of  the hunter warrior arrives thanks to her  scrapyard rescuer  dr dyson ido in order to satisfy the  pain he feels over his daughter's death  the doctor has registered with the  factory as a hunter warrior  he roams the streets at night defeating  vicious criminals in exchange for bounty  payments to fund his clinic  his weapon of choice is a rocket hammer  a gigantic blunt weapon with a rocket at  one end  that propels the device through its  target we only see the doctor fight  briefly in one skirmish before elita  jumps in  and dismantles his opponents with ease  if she hadn't been there though  we find it difficult to believe it would  have been successful with his cumbersome  weapon  the criminals in the alley are all  cyborgs and ido manages to knock off one  of their  limbs with his rocket hammer but after  this blow he stumbles while trying to  wield his massive weapon again  unless edo has spent years with a 100  success rate on his first fatal blow  it's hard to imagine that the kindly  doctor has the strength speed  and agility to be a successful hunter  warrior honestly  the poor guy can't even navigate through  a crowd without running into an innocent  bystander  given the impoverished citizens of iron  city's access to cybernetics  there must be some truly extraordinary  gadgets being used in xalam  we never truly see what life is like up  there but we do get a few details that  paint a vivid picture the fact that dr  edo  and dr shurin were forced into exile  because of their daughter's disease  indicates that death is shunned up there  in fact  nova's words spoken through his puppets  indicate access to outright immortality  just before elita thrusts her blade  through vector nova's voice creeps  through him to say  i found the only way to enjoy  immortality  is to watch others die on a first watch  the viewer is processing so much  information that this detail might slip  by without much notice  this line immediately follows the thug  gruwishka's defeat  and shortly after the reveal of dr  shurin's disassembled body  but a re-watch allows its implications  to sink in  as do elita's memories when they return  to her  they reveal that 300 years earlier she  was already battling nova  zalim residents seem to have access to  technology so advanced  they can achieve immortality while  maintaining much of their physical  humanity  meanwhile iron city's population is  forced to fuse their battered bodies  with whatever bits of old tech they can  scrounge up  while exploring the underwater wreckage  of a spaceship outside of iron city  elita finds a superior body which  possesses  lost technology from the united republic  of mars  initially ito refuses to attach elita to  this body  but after she's sliced apart in battle  he gives in  thus elita is fused with the berserker a  body of immense power and skill  when elite awakens in her new form she  shows off by executing a graceful  handstand  on her index finger after writing  herself she notices an intake flow on  her shoulder that generates arc plasma  at her finger it seems like an  unimportant if very cool  detail on a first watch one you might  assume is a nod to the original manga  but after seeing how everything plays  out towards the end of the film  you'll realize this device's true  purpose  after elita relieves the hunter warrior  zapan  of the ancient damascus blade she  displays the ability to engulf the  entire weapon  in a glowing plasma it is that little  blue flame  which she can now generate that pumps  power into the sword  and allows her to slice through  sentinels like butter  three centuries after the fall an  ultra-violent spore  called motorball dominates iron city  every kid grows up playing the sport  albeit with a little less death involved  elita is introduced to the game by hugo  and plays with the neighborhood kids  while learning how it all works  at its core motorball comes down to ball  possession and scoring  after watching the movie a couple times  however we're starting to think  scoring takes a back seat being the last  one standing  at least on the professional level when  we see a pro motorball match in action  some players do appear to chase the  elusive ball but many other players seem  to ignore it  interested only in ripping through their  opponents with whatever new age weaponry  the league has deemed legal  and if we're being honest we wouldn't  have it any other way  motorball without carnage would just be  robots on rollerblades  the grand arena is a place for these  futuristic gladiators to flex their  might  and satiate the public's lust for  violence  if they happen to toss that wonky ball  into the goal while shredding their  machine bodies  well that makes for extra bragging  rights but it really seems that the  point here  is to make it through the match without  getting your head ripped off  [Music]  the most obvious scene in elita battle  angel that points to a sequel  is nova's menacing reveal at the end of  the film  however there are numerous other details  hidden throughout the movie that hint  towards additional plots ripe for  expansion  one of the biggest occurs when elita is  being shown around the motorball track  by hugo when she asks who the best  player in the game  is hugo responds by saying that joshugen  is on track to be champion for less than  10 seconds  attention turns to the motorball player  in question as he receives repairs  it happens so quickly you might not  notice that joshugin  is played by jai courtney star of  suicide squad  divergent and terminator genesis an  actor known for his work in other  blockbuster franchises  is a nod to more being in store for this  character  in an interview with business insider he  recalled a conversation  he had with the film's director robert  rodriguez corning said  rodriguez called me up when they were in  production and said  there's this role it's a little small on  paper but if this thing blows up  i'll need someone who i can rely on when  we revisit it  that definitely tells us rodriguez has  much more in mind for courtney  should an elita sequel get the green  light  the seedy underbelly of iron city is run  by a man named vector  and his power stems from his corruption  of professional motorball  vector holds sway over the game's odds  by tweaking the player's power  going so far as to hire naive youth to  abduct and rob cyborgs of their limbs  his direct connection to xalam enables  such manipulation  he uses this relationship to make those  around him believe  he has the power to send people to the  floating city vector  dangles this promise in front of his  lackeys until they wise up and decide  they've had enough  it's at this moment that he fulfills his  end of the bargain and sends them to  zalem  albeit not in the way they'd hoped of  course if you've only watched elita once  you might not have latched on to this  detail  one example is when dr shurin decides to  quit her position  and vector tells her don't you think  it's time you want to zone  and i can send you up there right now  the next time we see shurin is after  elita crashes into  vector's office he says that he always  keeps his promises to send people to  xalam  just like dr shurin unfortunately he  then  opens up a chest revealing her brain and  other parts  ready to make its journey to the city in  the sky nova demands body parts for his  experiments and as vector says  that is the only way anyone gets to  xalam  there are a couple rules regarding what  weapons are allowed in the motorball  arena  but they're pretty lacks in fact after  watching the movie a few times you can't  help but notice how the sport transcends  the laws of iron city at large  guns are outlawed here hugo lays it all  out when informing elita  about weapons and the sword being  carried by zepan  all guns are outlawed in iron city  punishable by death  the need for unique weapons among the  hunter warriors makes sense  given this stipulation but what's with  all the deadly projectiles used by the  competitors in motorball  when elita is being chased down by an  entire team of bloodthirsty challengers  hellbent on placing her head on a pike  one of them fires a cannon at her  causing a massive explosion that knocks  elita off her feet  now we immediately picture bullet firing  pistols in regards to the no guns policy  but rocket launchers really seem like  they should fall into that illegal  category as well  the announcer of the match can be heard  mentioning legality and regulations  during the matches  but we're left thinking that might just  be for show  since the canon forms one player's  entire gigantic arm  the laws of iron city seem to be pretty  flexible  when elita displays the strength of her  new berserker body  dr ito has an appropriate response a  warrior's spirit needs a warrior's body  the synergy elita has with her new body  is indeed remarkable  the body boasts miraculous  nanotechnology once elita is attached to  the berserker  the entire system synchronizes with her  mind and begins making adjustments to  better represent her sense of self  this characteristic is subtly put on  display again  during the closing moments of the film  compared to how her berserker form  appears when she's first attached to it  the body that viewers are shown later is  much more attuned to combat  this hints at what elita has been  through in the months after hugo's death  chiefly she's fought her way through the  motorball league which is no  easy task thus her body is changed to  reflect her circumstances  it's a literal adaptation but also a  reflection  of elita's inner nature and her  boundless potential  you can't help but wonder what other  forms she might be able to take  perhaps in a sequel if fans of the film  get their wish  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies  are coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss  a single one  [Music]
 

